"""Single-point mutants of experiments/exp_astro_cyclefix.py (the guarded re-runs of the capped astronomy paths and the check of every other path: the side channel of the guard, the raw file, the freeze
check, the inventory and the scan for the cap, the layout of a re-run, the comparison with the stored run, write-once running, the report), for tools/mutants.py:

    venv/bin/python tools/mutants.py --exp exp_astro_cyclefix --tests tests/test_exp_astro_cyclefix.py --raw results/astro/cyclefix_raw.npz --md results/astro/cyclefix.md --out-env CYCLEFIX_OUT \\
        --extra tests/test_astro_report.py --extra results/astro/m2_raw.npz --extra results/astro/psf_raw.npz --extra results/astro/repeat_raw.npz --extra results/astro/freeze.json \\
        --extra results/astro/freeze_repeat.json --spec tools/mutants/wp_astrocyclefix_own.py --work <scratch dir> [--slot a --i0 0 --step 2]

A tuple is (id, what, old, new[, k]): `old` replaced by `new` at its k-th occurrence (0-based) in experiments/exp_astro_cyclefix.py. The kill criterion is the tests file alone.

Result (final run, slots a and b, 133 single-point mutants, kill criterion tests/test_exp_astro_cyclefix.py alone, 2026-11-08): 132 killed by the tests, 1 survivor (N03). The survivor is a
mutant whose effect is not visible in the stored files: N03 writes the record of the frozen state with every result instead of with the first one; the record is identical every time (a stored value may be
saved again if equal), so the raw file and the report are the same; an earlier partial run (N03 and Q07 only) had it killed by a test of that time that the final suite no longer has in that form, so it counts as a survivor of the final run. A test that watches the keys of every save
(test_run_jobs_writes_the_record_of_the_frozen_state_with_the_first_result_only) was added after the run and kills N03 (checked on its own together with the mutants Q05 and Q10, which the same change touches;
all three killed). 56 of the 133 mutants also changed the text of the report; the others change the runner, the file handling or the command line, which the report does not show. No equivalent survivor remains.
Run time of the whole mutation test about 50 min on two slots (about 30 s to 140 s per mutant: the slow ones are those that need a report of the real inventory).
"""
